{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/574618-plot-hooks-for-new-werewolf-pack-taking-new-territory","id":574618,"title":"Plot hooks for new werewolf pack taking new territory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-30T19:27:15-07:00","id":574618,"title":"Plot hooks for new werewolf pack taking new territory","content":"Hi all!<br /> <br /> i am about to start running a werewolf game set in Adelaide SA, where the pack is just being formed and given some largely uncontrolled territory including the eastern suburbs. the idea is these guys have popped up over the past little while, and now there is enough of them that the other packs are shoving them together to get them out of their hair. <br /> <br /> what i am looking for are some basic plot hooks, things to do while they learn the ropes of the game (this is the first major world of darkness game we're playing), while ultimately leading them to the climax of the first story - a spirit of road rage from the Britannia roundabout before it was changed (for those not from Adelaide, an awful intersection with far too many crashes that got improved over the past few years) is now starving, looking for a new high essence source of resonance, and is causing problems.<br /> <br /> i would also like to drop some hints of the azlu without full on pulling the reveal, cause that's something id like to play with later.<br /> <br /> still, for the first session i have...<br /> <br /> -find a totem, they already have roughly decided on it, but the first thing they'll do is locate it and solidify their pack<br /> <br /> -the britania roundabout itself, it was a highly negative place, not sure if it was a negative loci or a shoal (not quite bad enough for a wound.. but i may tongue in cheek that), which needs some maintenance to keep on the repair<br /> <br /> -a swarm of low level fear spirits generated from a recent string of murders (another recent game involving vampires and revenants) similar to fire spirits after a bushfire, are looking to try and stabilize, making people have panic attacks and such around the university of adelaide.<br /> <br /> -as they find a base of operations, they may notice this same person every so often lurking around (turns out to be a fire touched wolf blooded trying to suss out who is in the territory<br /> <br /> so, any other suggestions? they dont have to be specific to adelaide or anything, i can adapt. im just kind of new to werewolf and need some help<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6683-planbisnotbail","name":"PlanBIsNotBail","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:08:18-07:00","id":574774,"title":"","content":"Could do what I did. Hunters cleared the previous pack out. Get revenge, shut them down and move in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T21:04:03-07:00","id":575999,"title":"","content":"How long is this session? You have a lot of plot already.<br /> <br /> What helped me out a lot was handing the players their starting Aspirations and using them as Place Markers for the story. Um, for example you could wrap up one of the player's aspirations with getting across town. But have traffic get in the way. Traffic caused by the Road Rage Spirit. Intersect your plot with the Character's Aspirations. The Exp systems is built to help motivate your players to navigate their own personal narrative. Latch your Hooks on their motivation. Make your life easy. The plot will just flow naturally.<br /> <br /> As for your actual plot. Azlu might have sewn up the Gauntlet just after your Road Rage Spirit crossed, leaving it stuck. You can prep with both encounters leading to the other. If your players march after the Spirit first drop a verbal line from the Spirit about how the Gauntlet has become too strong to cross. If they happen upon some Azlu, have them skitter back to a Webbed Locus near the roadway the Spirit is feeding from.<br /> <br /> Maybe even juxtapose the Pack's intended Totem with the Spirit. Have both trapped out of the Hisil. Which begs that your young wolves address that problem immediately","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}